# build artifacts
# bin/ holds only make output; the single tracked file is the vendored
# static busybox consumed by tools/mkinitramfs.sh (not built by this repo).
bin/*
!bin/busybox-static
build/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.d
*.obj
*.ivpack

# volume images (never commit)
*.img
vm/

# release artifacts (make release)
dist/

# runtime logs
logs/
.ci-tools/

# external clone with own .git
tools/7-Zip-zstd/

# empty by design
downloads/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# generated docs bundle + playwright scratch
INVARIFS-DOCS.md
.playwright-mcp/

# WP22b flakey soak failure artifacts (backing images + logs)
tools/flakey/artifacts/

# codecpack helper binaries: rebuilt from the .c next to them by
# tools/test-<pack>.sh (cc -std=c11 ...) on every e2e run
tools/codecpacks/*/bin/

# generated video artifacts (regenerable: video/gen-overview.py + build.sh)
video/frames/
video/*.mp4
video/filter.txt

# local staging/VM trees (never track)
var/
*.d

# doxygen output (generated; make docs)
impl_docs/doxygen/

# LSP compilation database and editor configs
compile_commands.json
.clangd

# tools/lint-test-heredocs.sh scratch (should never land here, but if its
# path handling regresses again, do not let the blocks reach the index)
_tmp_tmp.*.py

# WP scratch dirs: a WP doc is deleted in its shipping commit (AGENTS.md 1.2).
# Never track one; `git add -A` from a worktree will otherwise sweep it in.
.wp*/

# WP129: the gzhdr seed corpus is generated by tools/mk-gzhdr-seeds.py
tools/fuzz/seeds/
# flakey failure artifacts: disk images a crashed run leaves behind, and the
# failed run leaves one EVERY TIME — 0.5-0.6 GB each on the root filesystem.
# That is not a hypothetical cost: it filled `/`, the harness could not write,
# and the session broke. The directory itself is now a SYMLINK to
# /srv/bench/moved/flakey-artifacts, so the bytes land on the 1.8T filesystem
# regardless; this line keeps the link out of `git status` so it is never swept
# in by `git add -A`.
tools/flakey/artifacts
# GitNexus-generated agent scaffolding (regenerate with: npx gitnexus analyze).
# CLAUDE.md stays ignored; .claude/ does NOT, because the committed AGENTS.md
# block cites .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md and a tracked file must not cite an
# ignored path -- that is exactly what made `repo hygiene` fail in CI with seven
# DOCROT lines while passing locally.

# .gitnexus/ is NOT entirely ignored. The 181 MB lbug graph store is, but
# run.cjs and gitnexus.json must ship: the committed AGENTS.md block and the
# committed .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md files both cite .gitnexus/run.cjs, and
# `repo hygiene` fails on a tracked file citing a missing path. This is the
# second time this exact shape bit us -- first .claude/ was ignored while
# AGENTS.md cited it, now .gitnexus/ is ignored while those cite it. A tracked
# file may not cite an ignored path, and the generated artifacts cite each
# other, so the shim has to be tracked even though the store must not be.
.gitnexus/lbug
.gitnexus/*.db
